"Royal Lee" <loneblinkr@nj.rr.com> writes:

> I've tried, but failed to find a spoiler explaining just exactly what stats
> effect what in the game. Could anyone explain, or post a link to show what
> Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma all
> effect? This would help a lot towards me understanding my character and
> playing them fully.

Here's what I've found after some source diving:

Strength affects:
Your carrying capacity
Your chance of hitting a monster in melee combat
The damage you do in melee combat
The time taken to set a bear trap
Your chance of kicking open a door or secret passage
The damage you do when kicking a monster
The distance you can kick or throw an object
The time taken to open a tin
Your chance of opening or closing a door
How effectively you dig or chew through shop walls

You cannot cast spells with Str less than 4.
You cannot jump or teleport at will with Str less than 6.
You cannot break a wand with Str less than 10.
You can only throw Mjollnir with Str 25.

Dexterity affects:
Your chance of hitting a monster in melee combat or with a spell
Your chance of kicking open a door or secret passage
Your chance of kicking a stuck item loose
The chance of rubbing out some of an engraving when standing on it
The time taken to set a trap
Your proficiency with a bullwhip
The damage you do when kicking a monster
Your chance of straining a muscle when kicking empty space
Your chance of hitting a monster with a missile (Dylan, this looks
like a bug in weap-343.txt)
Your chance of catching a returning boomerang
The time taken to open a tin
Your chance of opening or closing a door
The average time taken to unlock a door
The duration of wounded legs from a xan's attack
Your chance of getting special effects from a wooden flute or harp
Your chance of saddling a steed
Your chance of disarming a chest trap
Your chance of taking no time to begin two-weapon combat

If your Dex is less than 10, an attempt to move into a closed door
will bump into it.
Stunning spells cast by monsters have lesser duration if your Dex is
at least 12.

Constitution affects:
Your carrying capacity
Your healing rate
How many HP you gain when levelling up
Your time to live when sickened by a cursed unicorn horn or a
monster's sickness attack
The time taken to die from starvation
The damage taken when falling onto a sink
Your chance of escaping system shock when polymorphing

Your chance of kicking open a door or secret passage
The damage you do when kicking a monster
Your chance of opening or closing a door
(I'm not clear why Con matters for these last three)

If your Con is at least 16, you take less damage when hurting your
legs by kicking.

Intelligence affects:
Your chance of learning a spell
Your chance of casting a spell successfully (for most classes)
The damage you do when casting spells
How fast your PP regenerate
Your chance of having a positive foocubus encounter
Your chance of successfully using a crystal ball

Wisdom affects:
Your chance of casting a spell successfully (for some classes)
How fast your PP regenerate
How many PP you gain when levelling up

If your Wis is at least 13, floating eyes will freeze you for less
time.

Charisma affects:
The prices shopkeepers offer you
The amount of gold required to bribe soldiers
Your chance of saddling a steed
The chance of foocubi asking before removing your armour
Your chance of having a positive foocubus encounter

